1.e4 e5 {I decided to play the philidor again if my opponent will go for 1. e4, and if he would prepare - I will handle it}
2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 Be7 6.Be2 {He also went for this variation, which is the main move but I don't think it is the most challenging}
O-O 7.O-O Re8 8.f4 ( 8.Re1 {is the alternative, but he chose the same type of position as my previous opponent here}
) Bf8 9.Bf3 c5
{So up to here like the previous game I had in this variation, but here white
decided to deviate - I guess he was unprepared for it} 10.Nb3
( 10.Nde2 {is considered better} ) Nc6 11.Be3 ( 11.Re1 {is the main move - the innocent bishop move allows black a radical change of the structure, in his favor}
) Bf5 {! I remembered this move was played here by Gelashvili (against Guseinov -
this I did not recall), where draw was agreed soon, so I thought this cannot be
that bad. Also, I did not see any alternative I liked}
( 11...Bd7 {seemed too slow here, since white need not spend a tempo on h3 unlike the Nde2 case}
) ( 11...a5 12.a4 Nb4 {was an idea I knew of and considered here but it did not seem as strong to me}
) ( 11...d5
{!? is Bauer's recommendation which I did not recall and did not consider at
all. The computer gives white a slight advantage after} 12.exd5
Rxe3 13.dxc6 Qc7 ( 13...Qb6 14.Qd2 {was played by Smirin against Kuzmin, where after}
( 14.Nd2 {! is the best according to the computer, white is better} )
Rxf3 {!} 15.Rxf3 ( 15.gxf3 Qxc6 {with sufficient compensation according to Bauer}
( 15...Bh3 {! is even stronger} ) ) c4+ 16.Nd4 Bc5 {and the position is equal according to the computer - the game later ended in a draw}
) ) 12.exf5 {this is the best:} ( 12.Nd2 {?} d5 {! and black is much better}
) ( 12.Qd3 {?} Nb4 {and black is almost winning} )
( 12.Bxc5 {?! leads to black's advantage after} dxc5 {! stronger than taking on e4 which is also OK}
13.Qxd8 Rexd8 {! so the rook will not be attacked after B:c6! I of course missed this move}
( 13...Raxd8 14.exf5 c4 {?} ( 14...Nd4 {is equal} ) 15.Bxc6 bxc6
{necessary} 16.Na5 {and white is slightly better} ) 14.exf5 c4
{and black has huge compensation and is better} 15.Bxc6 cxb3
{! the point} 16.Ba4 bxa2 17.Rxa2 Bc5+ 18.Kh1 a6 {and the black pieces are much more active while the extra pawn is quite meaningless}
) Rxe3 13.g4 ( 13.Qd2 {and a draw was agreed here between Guseinov and Gelashvili; Black is better after}
Rxf3 {!!} 14.Rxf3 ( 14.gxf3 {is better, but who would play that?! and after}
Ne7 {black is still slightly better} ) d5 {! and black is better with more than sufficeint sompensation - the coordination of the white pieces is quite terrible}
( 14...c4 {is not as strong but also slightly better for black:}
15.Nd4 ( 15.Nc1 d5 {! the strongest, and black has great advantage}
( 15...Qb6+ {?!} 16.Kh1 Qxb2 {??} ( 16...d5 {! and black still has great advantage}
) 17.Rb1 {and suddenly white is much better} ) ) Qb6 16.Rd1 d5
17.Kh1 Re8 ) ) ( 13.Re1 {?} Rxe1+ 14.Qxe1 c4 {and black has great advantage}
) ( 13.Nd5 {is the best, and after} Nxd5 14.Qxd5 {and the position is equal:}
( 14.Bxd5 Qf6 {and black is better} ) Qb6 ( 14...Re8 15.c3 Ne7
16.Qxb7 Rb8 17.Qxa7 Nxf5 ) ( 14...Qf6 15.c3 ) ( 14...Ne7 15.Qd2
Nxf5 16.g4 Rxf3 17.Rxf3 {is in white's favor} ) 15.Rad1 Nb4
( 15...c4 16.Nd4 {is also about equal} ) 16.Qxb7 Qxb7 17.Bxb7
Rb8 18.Bf3 Nxc2 {is also about equal} ) d5 {! the best move - but played out of desperation, sort of...}
( 13...h6 14.g5 hxg5 15.fxg5 Nh7 16.h4 {did not appeal to me, although it turns out to be equal after}
( 16.g6 {! is stronger, with a very slight advantage to white} )
Nxg5 17.hxg5 Qxg5+ 18.Bg2 d5 19.Qd2 c4 20.Rae1 Rae8 )
( 13...Re8 14.g5 Nd7 {felt (and is indeed so) very good for white, who his much better}
) 14.Nxd5 {there is no alternative, especially in practice}
( 14.g5 d4 {is much better for black - it was clear to me even eithout calculation so I spent little time on this variation}
) ( 14.Bxd5 Rxc3 15.Bxc6 Qxd1 16.Rfxd1 Rxb3 {! is better for black} )
( 14.Nd2 {!? is the computer's suggestion, but who would play that? and it is clear black is better here:}
d4 15.Nce4 Nxe4 16.Bxe4 Nb4 ) Nxd5 {! after some thinking I decided on this}
( 14...Rxf3
{was in fact my original idea when I played d5: I didn;t like my position and
thought this will complicate matters and I will have sufficient compensation. This turns out to be wrong:}
15.Nxf6+ Qxf6 16.Qxf3 {!} ( 16.Rxf3 c4 {is indeed better for black} )
